  "notes": "Curation for tools/build-qqp.mjs (PROFECO QQP, city cdmx). Keys are the ids the pipeline prints: store id = slug of the chain FORMAT + sha1 of the normalised format|nombre comercial|dirección; product id = first two words of PRODUCTO + sha1 of the normalised producto|marca|presentación. renameChains maps every CADENACOMERCIAL label seen in the city (2025-2026) to the brand a shopper says (chain) and to PROFECO's format label (format); two labels with the same format are one store (PROFECO renamed 'Central de Abastos' to 'Central de Abasto' in May 2026, 111 stalls would otherwise be duplicated), so CHANGING A FORMAT CHANGES THE IDS OF ITS STORES (the reader's own prices are keyed by store id); a label missing here is shown and hashed as published. fixCoords holds only fixes that are certain from the data itself: tortilleria-tradicional-9bffbc (Tortillería Sin Nombre, Gustavo A. Madero) was published with longitude +99.11288 (sign missing); tortilleria-tradicional-859adc (Tortillería Hortelanos, Venustiano Carranza) with latitude -19.440087 (sign flipped). Not fixed, for a human: sears-b87bd0 (Sears Ecatepec) has longitude -101.158587 (Michoacán), the pipeline leaves it without a dot; bodega-aurrera-4a1ea3, bodega-aurrera-bb72d7, bodega-aurrera-771715 and bodega-aurrera-1bdbb4 have no coordinates at all in the source. fixSizes replaces the size parsed from PRESENTACIÓN for a product id ({ value, unit: g|ml|pza, pack?, why }, value = the package total), applied right after parsing and before any per-unit price, and counted in meta.json rules.fixSizes; use it only when the label itself states the size and the parser misreads it: lagricel-ofteno-b7bc82 'Caja con 4 Sobres Conteniendo Cada Uno 5 Ampolletas Aplicadoras con 0.5 Ml. C/U' was parsed 0.5 ml, it is 4 × 5 × 0.5 = 10 ml in 20 ampoules; biometrix-8c6488 '2 Cajas con Frasco con 30 Cápsulas C/U' was parsed 30, it is 2 × 30 = 60 capsules (research doc §20). Research: docs/research/profeco-qqp-2026-10.md."
